\textbf{Real-world results.} Figure~\ref{fig:real} shows that LLM-backbone methods beat RT-1 and Diffusion Policy on seen tasks (UP-VLA 0.80, UP-VLA-phi-w/o-mmu 0.75, UP-VLA-RT-2 0.65, RT-1 0.40, Diffusion Policy 0.30). For unseen-object grasping, UP-VLA-RT-2 (0.50) beats the model without MMU (0.30), consistent with the semantic benefit of VLM initialization, and UP-VLA is best at 0.60. For precise tasks the order flips, 0.35 for the model without MMU versus 0.20 for UP-VLA-RT-2, supporting the benefit of future prediction for spatial detail, and UP-VLA is best at 0.55.

