\textbf{Ablations.} Table~\ref{table:ablate} removes one component at a time. Removing prediction is most damaging on CALVIN (4.08 to 1.44) and lowers real-world seen and unseen success (0.80 to 0.65, 0.58 to 0.35). Removing Bridge pre-training reduces CALVIN to 2.74, so predictive pre-training on 25k Bridge demonstrations matters. Removing MMU barely changes CALVIN (3.89) or seen tasks (0.85) but drops unseen success from 0.58 to 0.20, so MMU mainly provides semantic generalization. Dropping the MMU-derived scene description from the action condition lowers CALVIN to 3.99 and unseen success to 0.50, so conditioning actions on it helps further. We report single numbers without variances, as none are given.

